    "notes": {
      "keep_rows": "Only completed interviews (HRESUL / HRESULT = 1; HH46 = 1 in 2019).",
      "row_ids_without_key": "The 2006-2013 public files have no identifiers: rows get their own ID and persons are not linked to households.",
      "map_columns": "The region comes from the province in 2006 (no region variable) and 2008 (its REGION has 4 codes that are not the 10 planning regions). 2008 covers only 7 provinces (Distrito Nacional, Santiago, Valverde, Duarte, Azua, Elías Piña, La Romana): it is not nationally representative and each region is only partly covered.",
      "relative_weight_years": "These years only have relative (normalized) weights: shares are valid, POPULATION / HOUSEHOLDS are left empty.",
      "derive_from_rules": "Completed education, one rule set per year (<level>C), first rule met: postgraduate, or university with 4+ years -> 4; university with fewer years, or media / secundaria with 4+ years -> 3; media with fewer years, or básica / primaria with 6+ grades -> 2; initial, none or fewer grades -> 1; never attended school (where asked) -> 1. 2006: a grade counts only when passed (P2018 = 1). 2018 uses H304C18 (2017 has the same names without the attendance question)."
    }
  }
